--- !u!114 &-3123979247667744889
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "Now let's see how the camera's Exposure is affected when entering <b>Volume Room 3.</b>\n\n1. With <b>Volume Room 3</b> selected, disable the Exposure override. Notice that the Scene gets darker.\r\n\r\n2. Undo your change.\r\n\r\nWhen the Exposure override for Room 3 is disabled, this area of the Scene inherits its Exposure settings directly from the <b>Global</b> volume. \r\n\r\nHowever, these particular settings might not be acceptable for a relatively dark room, such as Room 3. Therefore, a <b>Local</b> volume for Room 3 has been created, with dedicated Exposure overrides, among others.\r\n\r\nWhen the camera leaves <b>Volume Room 3,</b> the overrides that were set for this room will no longer be applied to the camera.\r"
