  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "Let\u2019s see how volumes are being used in this Scene.\r\n\r\n1. In the <i>Hierarchy,</i> expand <b>Lighting</b> > <b>Volumes.</b>\r\n\r\n2. Select the <b>Volume Global</b> GameObject.\r\n\n3. Notice the <b>Mode</b> is <b>Global</b> in the <i>Inspector.</i>\r\n\n4. Disable the <b>Tonemapping</b> Override. You can see that the image becomes more washed out as a result.\n\r\n5. Undo your change.\r\n\r\n<b>Global Volumes</b> have an effect on cameras, wherever they are located. This is important for setting up a baseline for effects that often remain constant thoughtout the scene, no matter the location of the camera, for instance:\n\u2022 Sky\n\u2022 Fog\n\u2022 Shadows\n\u2022 Tonemapping\n\u2022 Motion Blur\n\u2022 Film Grain \r"
